## Home dashboard

**Home** (`⌘0`) is the starting overview when you open Cardmaniacs or reset navigation. It synthesizes activity across feeds, Read Later, and bookmarks—not a separate content type.

Typical Home surfaces include:

- **Reading momentum** — recent activity and streak-style signals
- **Recommendations** — suggested items from your library with **Why this?** explanations where enabled
- **Quick entry** — jump into Unread, In Progress, or starred items
- **Discoverability** — surfacing neglected unread or in-progress cards

Home is editorial, not algorithmic social feed: recommendations draw from *your* library and reading patterns, not third-party trending topics.

{% note %}
Recommendation and “Why this?” copy depends on on-device intelligence and library size. New libraries show lighter dashboards until enough history exists.
{% /note %}

## Recommendations

When Apple Intelligence is available, Home may propose articles worth revisiting or finishing. Tap or select a recommendation to open the card in the reader. **Why this?** explains the ranking in plain language—recent stars, in-progress status, feed relevance, or similar signals.

Dismiss or ignore recommendations freely; they do not mutate read state until you act.

## Statistics

Reading **statistics** track how you use Cardmaniacs over time—articles read, time in reader, queue throughput, and related metrics exposed in the analytics feature.

Access statistics via:

- **Home** widgets and links
- **Go to Statistics** in the command palette (Read Later context)
- In-app statistics views where shown on your platform

### Export

The app can **export reading stats** (CSV or formats exposed in settings) for personal tracking—year-in-review spreadsheets, accountability logs, or migration to external tools. Export entry points live in statistics UI and **Settings → Advanced** data sections where enabled.

{% tip %}
Export before major library cleanup if you want historical records of reading volume.
{% /tip %}

## Relationship to other destinations

| Destination | Role |
|-------------|------|
| Home (`⌘0`) | Overview + recommendations |
| Feeds (`⌘1`) | Incoming published items |
| Read Later (`⌘2`) | Your queue |
| Statistics collection | Deep metrics slice of queue activity |

Home is the wrong place to triage fifty unread feed items—use Triage layout on Feeds instead. Home answers *what should I pick up next?*

## Habits that keep Home useful

1. Mark read (`⌘E`) when finished—stats and recommendations stay accurate
2. Archive palette-clear items you will not reopen
3. Star (`⌘⇧S`) genuinely important pieces recommendations can respect
4. Review **In Progress** weekly via palette Go To

## Privacy

Statistics are computed from local and iCloud-synced library data. Exports are user-initiated files on your device—Cardmaniacs does not upload a separate analytics profile to a proprietary server for Home.

